# serial_cycle_wide_mute -- shared memory with no doorbell over it, and the
# reason the other half of the concurrency test is needed too.
#
# serial_cycle_wide_wired showed a channel across a pair that shares no
# region. This declaration is its mirror: `spill` is a small store `alder`
# writes and `cedar` reads, and no channel joins them at all. They share
# memory in silence.
#
# A concurrency test that read only the channels would wave that pair
# through, exactly as a test reading only the grants waved the wired pair
# through. Two domains may run at once when they share no region AND no
# channel; each test alone is a half-answer, and this document and the
# wired one are the two halves proving it.
#
# The shape pays for the extra region, and honestly. alder now touches
# birch, dogwood, and cedar, so it spans three peers and the walk no longer
# closes on every domain once -- this is a ring with a shortcut across it
# rather than a ring, which is what serial_cycle_bypass already taught. So
# inside a true ring the two tests always agree, since a region joining two
# domains makes them neighbors; they separate only in a shape like this one.
#
# Read whole by `caravan/read.rye`; measured, never run, by
# `caravan/concurrent.rye`.

system serial_cycle_wide_mute

domain alder
domain birch
domain cedar
domain dogwood

channel alder birch
channel birch cedar
channel cedar dogwood
channel dogwood alder

region ask_ab 4096
region ask_bc 4096
region ask_cd 4096
region ask_da 4096
region taken 64
region spill 64

grant ask_ab alder rw
grant ask_ab birch r
grant ask_bc birch rw
grant ask_bc cedar r
grant ask_cd cedar rw
grant ask_cd dogwood r
grant ask_da dogwood rw
grant ask_da alder r
grant taken alder rw
grant taken dogwood r
grant spill alder rw
grant spill cedar r
